Recommanded 7/10.

This is the 2nd best videogame narrative there is, behind Planesape: Torment. It breaks the fourth wall in a way that no other game does; it delievers a moral tale that says as much about the messy nature of modern conflict as it does about all media's attempts to glorify war and cover up it's indecencies. That being said there is one thing that needs to be made absolutely clear before anyone goes in and becomes disappointed; 

The narrative complexity of this game is almost completely lacking in the first half of the game, ~8 chapters. In hindsight, it's clear there's a lot of foreshadowing going on, but your first time through, the first 8 chapters of Spec Ops: The Line appears to be one of the blandest CoD rip offs on Steam, and while I do believe this was purely intentional, to really drive the nature of the 2nd half, it is important that you understand this before getting tired and dropping the game at chapter 7.

I would also recommend playing on easy, because, frankly, the gameplay is kinda boring, and you more likely than not will die more often that you want even on easy.

I am utterly impressed. At first, I could not believe another shoot-them-all game would change my view on the genre. So, feeling quite sceptically, I purchased it and prepared for another meaningless mix of violence and cursing.

Well, there was a lot of violence and cursing indeed. However, it was flavoured with a great concept of a single man creating his own world. His own war. His own enemies. And, after all, sacrificing his people for the sake of his own illusions.  

Frankly, I find the Spec Ops relatively close to the Bioshock Infinite. It is far more than shooting. Both games are about seeking the truth and realising that there is no truth. There is reality. Or plenty (in case of Bioshock).

But let me get back to the matter of this particular game. Amongst all shooters that I have played, this one I doubtlessly call the #1. That I do for that the game possesses all of the following:
1. Great storyline;
2. High-quality graphics;
3. Distinctive characters;
4. Lots of shooting;
5. Handy gameplay;
6. Right of choice;
7. Unexpected ending.

What do I have to say for conclusion? I certainly recommend this game to everyone who values both engaging story and exciting action. A must-play!

It is a good game, full of action and bullets all the time.
Pros:
+ game mechanics is good, with easy actions for shooting or granedes;
+ different weapons and shooting effects;
+ beautiful landscape and rich in details;
Cons:
- very violent and gore, some images might be disturbing for naive/innocent minds;
- short, did it in 6-7 hours including breaks;
- (small spoiler on this line) the decisions that you take don't change the playing experience;
